Z||000000||DreXteR||10-29-2000||10:53 PM||||My friend said that a Nos system its preferible than a turbo one. Well, I like more the turbines, but if its true the nos system its better, then I will go 4 it.  The thing is that I will rebuild the engine and the compression for a turbo have to be 8.5. And I want to make a preformance rebuild, perf cams, vlave springs, heads machine work, and so on...<P>An issue is a 3.2 convertion, depends on wich way I decide to go(turbo or nos) is the kind of rebuild I will make.  I read in somewhere in the web that a sc setup pump to 200 hp in a dyno! Thats good, a turbine @ the same psi have to make the same power if not more. Im aiming to +300hp (if its possible) with turbo and performance rebuild. Maybe can be possible to add a nos with the turbine(an overkill 4 sure, but possible with the rigth parts).<P>I need help here guys!. Need to go in the rigth way.||||reg||4
Z||000001||Shiner||10-29-2000||11:43 PM||||Drexter,<P> It really comes down to you and your style of driving.  Do you take it easy most of the time, and only get on the car hard during bursts, like drag racing? If so, the blue bottle would be right up your alley. Or do you like to drive the car hard and fast all the time?  Turbo would be prefered there, otherwise you will be running out of juice all the time.<P> So think about what YOU want out of this rebuild.<P>------------------<BR>-Shiner-<BR>'84 Sport Coupe<BR>'87 GT<BR>'86 SE 2M6 (parts car)<p>[This message has been edited by Shiner (edited 10-29-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||DaRkLoRD||10-30-2000||12:12 AM||||How much would a 50 HP NOS kit be, and how much does it cost to fill a bottle?<P>I tend to drive hard most of the time.. so if a year of using NOS is gonna cost the same as a turbo, I might get that instead.. I've been planning on getting NOS on my GT next year..<P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||5
Z||000003||1FST2M6||10-30-2000||08:15 AM||||a 70hp shot is about $500 and cost $30 to fill a bottle. where a turbo cost $3200 plus install. <P>------------------<BR>Shhh.. Top Secret! <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fstcheeto_2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Formula 18||10-30-2000||11:05 AM||||You can put together a turbo kit for under a grand if you get the pieces your self. Denis LaGura (sp?) has a web site on how to do it using a Garrett T-3 turbo off a Thunderbird coupe (about $75). He run about ten pounds boost and now has a 3.4 turbo thatis BUILT and is stoopid fast (that one's a little more) ||||reg||1
Z||000005||88formula||10-30-2000||05:19 PM||||The good thing about a turbo is that the power never runs out and there are no bottles to fill, which cost money.||||reg||1
Z||000006||BigTurbo87GT||10-30-2000||06:00 PM||||I love the sound of a Turbo spooling up and the blow off valve swooshing between shifts!<BR>Only cool factor of NOS is when you vent the lines.<BR>All my opinions are strictly Opinionated.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Sleeper||10-30-2000||08:17 PM||||Every mag I have ever read says turbo is is the most RELIABLE of the three (turbo/supercharger/nos) and nos is always ranked 3rd, if you wanna go fast fast you have to be willing to pay the $$$ to do so, don't go cheap and buy the lowly nos, when it will burn out your motor way sooner than the other 2. ||||reg||1
Z||000008||DreXteR||10-31-2000||02:03 AM||||Thanx Guys!.  <P>I like to drive hard and fast!!  This is my weekend car, so it dont be treated bad.  I just want to make the best of my fiero, like everybody wants. I think the turbo is the best bet for me. I like the punch of a power car, make me feel like a roller coaster  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <P>BTW, what about the compresion needed for a turbo engine?  My friend told me the the highest compresion is 8.5:1 .  If I will make a 3.2 mod, the compresion will be 8.5:1 or I can go farter, like 9.5:1?  Im planing to get some forged pistons, a 3.1 crack, maybe an SI valve kit(if worth it, performance related), perf cam, cil heads work(reshape, ported in/out, high presure oil pump, crane vlave springs and retainers, and so on.  With this type of rebuild I can use a turbo?  <P>Thanx for all the help.<BR>  ||||reg||10
Z||000009||1FST2M6||10-31-2000||09:04 AM||||you can have 12:1 and still have a turbo you'll just need LOTS of fuel and water injection. but the lower the compression the more boost you can run on PUMP gas. 8.5:1 would be GREAT for 15psi as long as its inter cooled. you'll have decent torque off boost for tooling around in traffic and you'll have the ability to BOOST THE HELL OUT OF IT for track use! you'll need an MSD 6BTM and a Vortech SFMU for ignition and fuel both units are boost sensative and well worth the money! <P>------------------<BR>Shhh.. Top Secret! <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fstcheeto_2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
