Z||000011||DaRkLoRD||10-31-2000||12:35 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by N_Man:<BR><B>Hey Formula 18,  Is there any chance of digging up that website?  I wouldnt mind taking a peruse throught it. Thanks</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P> <A HREF="http://members.xoom.com/dlagrua/turbo.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://members.xoom.com/dlagrua/turbo.htm</A> <P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||3
Z||000012||Greg Piet||10-31-2000||01:38 PM||||Now why oh why is a turbo ranked higher than a supercharger...   The turbo lag I would think would put a turbo in 2nd place.<P>I am guessing the extra drain on the motor from a supercharger is why a turbo is ranked higher??||||reg||1
Z||000013||zeusrekning||10-31-2000||03:48 PM||||can anyone describe "turbo lag"?||||reg||1
Z||000014||1FST2M6||10-31-2000||03:53 PM||||the time from when you stomp on the pedal to the time your head is SMASHED AGINST THE SEAT. no boost to full boost.  a positive displacement S/C make STOOPID torque(no lag), a Centrifugal makes STOOPID HP(lag). but a turbo makes booth if tuned right and has little or no parasitic drain on the engine.(lag) ||||reg||1
Z||000015||Formula 18||10-31-2000||04:50 PM||||Fast 2m6- Doesn't accell make a Igintion model with an add on computer that will adjust timing under boost and set timing on too? <P>DreXteR- unles you plan on running MAJOR boost you can pretty much stick to stock compression ratio. The higher compression that more fuel you'll need under boost. However bigger injectors can cause all kinds of problems when your not running boost.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000016||Wannabe||10-31-2000||08:17 PM||||Turbos are the best for ultimate power potential, but can be more difficult to tune for good drivability on the street. The engine management systems available these days make it possible to get very good drivability from a turbo though. Tuning can be tricky too, because the speed/airflow relationship is not as linear as a supercharger. An s/c makes smaller engines feel like big engines, but robs some of the power it helps produce. For example, 3800 s/c engine in the GTP actually puts out about 300hp, but about 60 hp is used up to drive the supercharger. For street driving, it really comes down to personal preference. Personally, I think nothing beats the rush of a turbo kicking in  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000017||DreXteR||10-31-2000||09:16 PM||||Formula 18- Im planing go to 15 psi, thinking in 3.4 injectors too to compensate the air mass from the turbine. For normal driving use 5-8 psi and race drive pump to 15 psi. Thats why I was thinking in use forged pistons, to make the motor ron safe under heavy presure.  I dont want to kill it   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P><BR>1st2m6-  Can I use a performance cam with a turbine? and use other sort of performace parts with it?<BR>I ask this 'cause my friend told me that if I use a performance cam(ex. compucam), the engine can broke or not function propertly with a turbine.  <P>Somebody have some facts of SI valves regarding power gained or performance factor?<P>Thanx for the help!!<BR>||||reg||10
Z||000018||1FST2M6||11-01-2000||08:13 AM||||the Accel DFI can be mated to a + pressure map but it is not boost sensative.. it will keep a constant path. you'll need to add on to the DFI the MSD 6BTM and Vortech SFMU. I Had SI valves in my 86 SE (GT Bastard has it now) and they are great! if they'll take 16+ bottles of nitrous they'll last through anything. and your friend doesn't know what hes talking about.. a biger beter cam is just that BETTER! your exhaust can NEVER be to big on a Turbo car.. the less back pressure you have the faster it'll spool up and the less turbo lag you'll have. A good fordged piston is great Arias, Weisco, JE. TRW are rather heavy compared to the others. Try and stay away from Hypereutectic. just in case you want to add Nitrous one day. 15psi is do able with 9.5:1 compression or lower any thing over that you'll have detonation problems and you'll need an intercooler AND water injection  <A HREF="http://www.f-max.com" TARGET=_blank>www.f-max.com</A>    hope this helps...    if you'd like a little reassurance.. I help build the cars on the front page.. Paulo, and Nates Turbo Intercooled B16a1 Civics  <A HREF="http://www.engineered.net" TARGET=_blank>www.engineered.net</A>  If you need a turbo let me know the shop is a stocking Turbonetics Dealer. <A HREF="http://www.turboneticsinc.com" TARGET=_blank>www.turboneticsinc.com</A> <P> <A HREF="http://resource.crx.org/feature" TARGET=_blank>http://resource.crx.org/feature</A>   they are pulling 500+hp out of 9.0:1 with 18psi.. imagine a 3.2 with the same  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 11-01-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000019||N_Man||11-01-2000||09:06 PM||||Just curious, but i always thought if your cam was to agressive that it would interupt the smooth flow of exaust,  therefore increasing turbo lag especially at low RPM.<P>Say would a compucam2030 be appropriate for a boosted engine||||reg||1
Z||000020||DreXteR||11-03-2000||12:27 AM||||With the stock engine a turbo can give @least 80 hp, If I make the performance rebuild it will give 80 or more hp's?<P>||||reg||1
